  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 240 PM CDT Wed Sep 30 2026\n\nFor this weekend, we are expecting drier conditions, seasonable\ntemperatures, and overall, fall-like weather. This will be \ncontributed by zonal flow progressing across the northern CONUS,\nsurface high pressure systems to our north, and the development\nof a 500mb high pressure system in the desert southwest. For \nSaturday, a surface high pressure will be over the Great Lakes, \nand will continue to progress eastward. We will still see its \ninfluence with temperatures in the upper-60s to low-70s, cooler \novernight temperatures, and a southeasterly wind. On Sunday, a \n500mb high pressure center will further develop and contribute \nto height rises, resulting in a ridge to build over the western \npart of the CONUS. Our area will be downstream of the ridge \naxis, and with the addition of another surface high pressure \nsystem over southern Canada, winds will shift to a northerly \ndirection, and help continue seasonable temperatures. Drier \nconditions, and temperatures typical for this time of year are \nexpected to stick around into next week.",
